# Auto-flash firmware

After changing anything that ships on the ESP32 (`firmware/main/`, `firmware/CMakeLists.txt`, `firmware/sdkconfig*`, partitions — not `firmware/host_test` alone), **build and flash before finishing**. Do not leave a firmware change unflashed.

ESP-IDF is the Docker image `espressif/idf:v5.4.2` (not a host `IDF_PATH`).

```bash
# build
docker run --rm \
  -v "$PWD/firmware:/project" -w /project \
  espressif/idf:v5.4.2 idf.py build

# flash (no monitor — it blocks)
PORT=$(ls /dev/ttyUSB* 2>/dev/null | head -1)
PORT=${PORT:-$(ls /dev/ttyACM* 2>/dev/null | head -1)}
docker run --rm --device="$PORT" \
  -v "$PWD/firmware:/project" -w /project \
  espressif/idf:v5.4.2 idf.py -p "$PORT" flash
```

- Prefer **`/dev/ttyUSB*`** (CP2102 UART). Fall back to **`/dev/ttyACM*`** (native USB Serial/JTAG).
- If ACM is busy, Chrome Web Serial has it. Ask the user to **Disconnect** in the dashboard, then flash. Do not skip.
- If no board is present, say so. The firmware task is not done.
- Do not run `monitor` unless the user asks.
